WEBVTT

00:00:40.040 --> 00:00:42.500
Oh, so here is where you are, El.

00:00:42.500 --> 00:00:44.160
Mm-hmm.

00:00:44.160 --> 00:00:46.790
Didn't you hear your dad calling you?

00:00:46.790 --> 00:00:50.790
I heard you, but I'm at a really good part.

00:00:50.790 --> 00:00:54.450
What are we going to do
about your appetite for books?

00:00:55.790 --> 00:00:58.410
What are you reading this time?

00:01:00.700 --> 00:01:03.950
<i>Sherlock Holmes</i>.

00:01:03.950 --> 00:01:07.950
I just don't find detectives to be to my liking.

00:01:13.290 --> 00:01:19.410
This is the tale of the man who confounded
even the great detective Sherlock Holmes...

00:01:26.540 --> 00:01:31.000
Professor Moriarty, the Lord of Crime.

00:01:44.120 --> 00:01:46.950
<i>The mist is hiding the sin</i>

00:01:46.950 --> 00:01:49.700
<i>I hold in my hand the LIST of judgment</i>

00:01:49.700 --> 00:01:52.330
<i>I'm gonna do the perfect crime</i>
<i>and bury them in a cist</i>

00:01:52.330 --> 00:01:57.620
<i>That's my DYING WISH for you</i>
<i>(Set a thief to catch another thief)</i>

00:01:57.620 --> 00:02:03.040
<i>Guys of the privileged class torment the weak</i>
<i>(Set a thief to catch another thief)</i>

00:02:03.040 --> 00:02:06.120
<i>And they enjoy it</i>

00:02:06.120 --> 00:02:11.660
<i>That's a bloody world, an endlessly</i>
<i>discriminatory society (dystopia)</i>

00:02:11.660 --> 00:02:16.660
<i>Happiness does not bloom here</i>
<i>(Set a thief to catch another thief)</i>

00:02:16.660 --> 00:02:19.790
<i>We are oppressed</i>

00:02:19.790 --> 00:02:25.370
<i>We must do something. Come on</i>

00:02:25.370 --> 00:02:31.830
<i>Let the end begin</i>

00:02:31.830 --> 00:02:37.700
<i>Break it to relieve your soul</i>

00:02:37.700 --> 00:02:43.620
<i>Open your eyes. You'll be reborn</i>
<i>when you lose your life</i>

00:02:43.620 --> 00:02:48.700
<i>Lord of crime hora yume no ikenie</i>
<i>We're lords of crime. We're sacrifice for ideals</i>

00:02:48.700 --> 00:03:00.950
<i>Freedom lives forever, even if we die</i>

00:04:47.120 --> 00:04:51.200
"The Earl's Crime"

00:04:58.750 --> 00:05:01.750
Now there's been a seventh victim.

00:05:01.750 --> 00:05:06.200
"The townsfolk tremble
at the faceless assailant."

00:05:09.250 --> 00:05:12.250
It's a dreadful affair, William.

00:05:12.250 --> 00:05:15.870
Yeah. They exclusively target
young boys for their amusement,

00:05:15.870 --> 00:05:19.290
and then, after they're done, slaughter them.

00:05:19.290 --> 00:05:22.330
It's hard to believe a human being
could do such a thing.

00:05:24.700 --> 00:05:29.910
It's human to think that this
could not be the work of man.

00:05:32.290 --> 00:05:37.080
"Dissatisfaction toward the police is growing
as the culprit remains at large."

00:05:37.080 --> 00:05:41.410
Apparently, there aren't any clues,
and the police have nothing to go on.

00:05:41.410 --> 00:05:42.870
Oh, but there <i>are </i>clues.

00:05:42.870 --> 00:05:44.120
Huh?

00:05:44.120 --> 00:05:46.290
Within this article.

00:05:50.080 --> 00:05:54.120
Looking at the child victims and
the occupations of their parents,

00:05:54.120 --> 00:05:56.370
do you notice anything that stands out?

00:05:59.290 --> 00:06:00.950
A clock smith...

00:06:02.580 --> 00:06:04.040
A hatter...

00:06:05.250 --> 00:06:07.540
A jeweler...

00:06:07.540 --> 00:06:10.120
A horse keeper...

00:06:10.120 --> 00:06:12.620
A tailor...

00:06:12.620 --> 00:06:18.000
And now, whilst his father's business
is unknown, we have a messenger boy.

00:06:19.250 --> 00:06:23.200
People's fancies do not get taken
by that which is out of view.

00:06:23.200 --> 00:06:25.830
They want what they see.

00:06:27.120 --> 00:06:30.750
Louis, the omelettes you make are exquisite.

00:06:30.750 --> 00:06:35.500
Even when I am in the field,
whenever I get hungry, that's what I crave.

00:06:35.500 --> 00:06:38.790
Well, thanks.

00:06:38.790 --> 00:06:43.370
But then, yes, take the example
of people in the orient,

00:06:43.370 --> 00:06:47.040
ignorant that a dish called
an omelette even exists.

00:06:47.040 --> 00:06:50.080
I doubt they would ever get
such a craving for one.

00:06:51.450 --> 00:06:55.200
The occupations I listed earlier
all come in contact quite often

00:06:55.200 --> 00:06:59.950
with members of the nobility,
or those of corresponding upper classes.

00:07:01.370 --> 00:07:07.000
Whenever a nobleman purchases meat,
he never enters the butcher shop himself.

00:07:07.000 --> 00:07:08.660
However...

00:07:08.660 --> 00:07:15.200
They do visit the shops to pick out jewellery,
and go to the stables to board their carriages.

00:07:15.200 --> 00:07:20.830
Correct. And there may be opportunity
to see members of their families there.

00:07:20.830 --> 00:07:22.580
It is not unusual for a shopkeeper's son

00:07:22.580 --> 00:07:26.290
to assist with their father's
work as an apprentice.

00:07:27.370 --> 00:07:32.250
Nor for them to encounter messenger boys
at the clubs to which they belong.

00:07:32.250 --> 00:07:38.950
Yes. Our culprit does not wander to and fro
in search of his preferred prey.

00:07:38.950 --> 00:07:43.790
He has entertained his appetites with those
he sees in his own sphere of life.

00:07:44.830 --> 00:07:49.200
People want what they see.

00:07:49.200 --> 00:07:52.540
Two or three might have
been simply a coincidence.

00:07:52.540 --> 00:08:00.250
However, once it rises to five or six,
those odds grow profoundly lower.

00:08:00.250 --> 00:08:01.830
Then you mean...

00:08:03.290 --> 00:08:07.120
This may be a case in which we become involved.

00:08:11.080 --> 00:08:14.040
Still, one of the victims...

00:08:14.040 --> 00:08:18.500
...appears to have been an orphan
who slept on the streets. What of him?

00:08:18.500 --> 00:08:22.750
Ah, yes. Noblemen and orphans--
there is nothing quite so far removed

00:08:22.750 --> 00:08:25.660
as the two worlds in which they live.

00:08:25.660 --> 00:08:32.450
Assuming that's the case, it could be
the clue that leads us to our culprit.

00:08:55.870 --> 00:08:59.250
Why, Lord Albert...

00:08:59.250 --> 00:09:04.200
It is my pleasure to welcome you to my shop.
What can I do for you today?

00:09:04.200 --> 00:09:08.580
The tuxedo you ordered will not
be ready for some time yet.

00:09:08.580 --> 00:09:13.040
No, that isn't why I'm here today.

00:09:13.040 --> 00:09:16.620
Allow me to express my condolences
for what happened to Roddy.

00:09:23.000 --> 00:09:26.450
If you'd have let me know,
I would have attended his funeral.

00:09:26.450 --> 00:09:28.120
Out of the question.

00:09:28.120 --> 00:09:34.790
You, Lord Albert, an earl, coming to the funeral
of commoners such as ourselves?

00:09:37.750 --> 00:09:43.120
You're looking a bit careworn.
Shouldn't you be getting some rest?

00:09:43.120 --> 00:09:45.540
I am very touched by your concern.

00:09:45.540 --> 00:09:50.290
However, working helps me
to keep my mind off of my grief.

00:09:51.500 --> 00:09:56.330
I saw him here in the store a number
of times. Roddy was a good lad.

00:09:56.330 --> 00:10:01.120
Yes. If you will pardon me,
speaking as his father,

00:10:01.120 --> 00:10:04.540
he was an obedient, dutiful young boy.

00:10:04.540 --> 00:10:08.910
How could he have met such a gruesome fate?

00:10:10.950 --> 00:10:12.750
Supposing...

00:10:16.120 --> 00:10:19.290
...I knew who did this to him...

00:11:02.750 --> 00:11:05.580
I'd like to have a brief word with you.

00:11:06.660 --> 00:11:08.080
Would you mind?

00:11:16.750 --> 00:11:20.540
Sorry to make such a mess in front of you, sir.

00:11:20.540 --> 00:11:23.700
So, what is it you wanted to ask me?

00:11:23.700 --> 00:11:27.000
Your instrument there--
it wasn't always yours, was it?

00:11:30.370 --> 00:11:36.250
For it being your livelihood,
you do not seem accustomed to playing it.

00:11:36.250 --> 00:11:38.830
Sir, you're not a cop, are you?

00:11:38.830 --> 00:11:43.120
Don't be silly. If I were,
I wouldn't be so indirect about this.

00:11:43.120 --> 00:11:45.450
Hmm, I guess so.

00:11:45.450 --> 00:11:49.120
They haul you off to the station
before talking to you.

00:11:51.580 --> 00:11:53.870
This is Cass's.

00:11:55.330 --> 00:11:57.160
You know about what's happening, right?

00:11:57.160 --> 00:12:00.910
It's because of that that Cass
ended up like he did.

00:12:00.910 --> 00:12:05.910
Anyhow, I'm his mate,
so I inherited his business, see?

00:12:06.910 --> 00:12:11.580
Anyhow, that spot was unlucky for him,
so I found a different corner.

00:12:11.580 --> 00:12:16.160
So then, where did Cass make his living?

00:12:16.160 --> 00:12:21.830
Oh, that would be... the road
two streets over from where I was.

00:12:29.250 --> 00:12:31.410
He was spotted from a carriage?

00:12:31.410 --> 00:12:34.620
No, if he was spied as prey,

00:12:34.620 --> 00:12:38.000
there would have been opportunity
to study him more thoroughly.

00:12:48.330 --> 00:12:52.500
Then, the culprit saw him from that window?

00:12:52.500 --> 00:12:55.830
The chances are quite high.

00:12:55.830 --> 00:13:00.870
He could not look away from the beggar boy
on the street beneath his gaze,

00:13:00.870 --> 00:13:03.120
is that what happened?

00:13:03.120 --> 00:13:05.450
Whose house is that?

00:13:05.450 --> 00:13:11.450
Oh, it isn't a private residence.
It's a clubhouse for the Gastros Club.

00:13:11.450 --> 00:13:14.040
The Gastros Club?

00:13:14.040 --> 00:13:17.620
That's a place frequented by
wealthy connoisseurs of good food.

00:13:17.620 --> 00:13:21.290
Oh, Albert, you know of it?

00:13:21.290 --> 00:13:24.000
I don't hear very many good things about it,

00:13:24.000 --> 00:13:27.870
but I do have a number of acquaintances
who are members there.

00:13:27.870 --> 00:13:30.200
That is quite advantageous.

00:13:30.200 --> 00:13:35.370
In order to join the club,
one must have a member referral.

00:13:35.370 --> 00:13:38.040
William, does this mean...?

00:13:38.040 --> 00:13:44.200
Yes. Now that so many indicators point to there,
we cannot very well ignore it.

00:13:49.620 --> 00:13:55.750
In that case, we may be able to provide Eden
with a chance for vengeance.

00:14:06.660 --> 00:14:07.620
Ah, you there...

00:14:07.620 --> 00:14:09.790
Yes, what can I do for you?

00:14:09.790 --> 00:14:13.500
Who is that gentleman who always
sits over by the window?

00:14:13.500 --> 00:14:17.330
Ah, that would be the Earl of Argleton.

00:14:17.330 --> 00:14:21.580
I am told that he is one of
the club's founding members.

00:14:21.580 --> 00:14:27.660
Does that mean that the earl has had that
seat reserved since the founding of the club?

00:14:27.660 --> 00:14:30.450
No, that is not the case.

00:14:30.450 --> 00:14:35.250
However, the earl usually sits there
whenever it is available.

00:14:40.410 --> 00:14:42.330
Your lordship...

00:14:43.660 --> 00:14:49.950
It is my pleasure to meet you.
My name is William James Moriarty.

00:14:49.950 --> 00:14:52.750
Do you need something from me?

00:14:52.750 --> 00:14:56.330
No, I would not say I need anything.

00:14:56.330 --> 00:15:02.540
You just looked somewhat bored sitting here,
so I thought I might engage you in conversation.

00:15:02.540 --> 00:15:04.660
No, I'm really not...

00:15:04.660 --> 00:15:09.790
That suit is one you had tailored
from Eden's, is it not?

00:15:09.790 --> 00:15:12.290
And your ring--

00:15:12.290 --> 00:15:19.160
the mounting is a bit elaborate, but it was
crafted by Goldstein Jewellers, yes?

00:15:19.160 --> 00:15:23.410
You have quite the observant eye.
Almost like a detective.

00:15:23.410 --> 00:15:25.750
Shall I keep guessing?

00:15:25.750 --> 00:15:30.540
The pocket watch you are now wearing
came from R. Masters Clock Smith.

00:15:30.540 --> 00:15:32.160
Am I correct?

00:15:32.160 --> 00:15:37.580
My word, how can you tell where my pocket
watch is from without even seeing it?

00:15:37.580 --> 00:15:40.870
Your hat is from Morgan Bros. Company.

00:15:40.870 --> 00:15:45.040
The horses you own are stabled
at the Shannon Racing Club.

00:15:46.660 --> 00:15:52.500
Further, you have taken an interest
in the tones of the concertina of late.

00:15:56.950 --> 00:16:00.120
You prefer the meat of young hares, yes?

00:16:00.120 --> 00:16:06.250
Tender, not yet fully developed,
and so fresh that it still drips with blood,

00:16:06.250 --> 00:16:10.750
which you take your time
to savour, nice and slow.

00:16:12.370 --> 00:16:16.830
One other thing--you do not appear
to be very good at playing cards.

00:16:18.290 --> 00:16:21.830
Your inner thoughts are reflected
all too readily upon your face.

00:16:25.500 --> 00:16:29.620
Excuse me, I just remembered
an urgent matter I must attend to.

00:16:59.290 --> 00:17:01.910
You were told to follow me
and find out who I am.

00:17:01.910 --> 00:17:05.870
Or perhaps, your instructions
were to dispatch me at once.

00:17:07.870 --> 00:17:10.540
You seem to be accustomed to fisticuffs,

00:17:10.540 --> 00:17:13.370
but you would do well
to use your head a bit more.

00:17:13.370 --> 00:17:17.830
This isn't like when you kidnap
defenceless children, after all.

00:17:19.040 --> 00:17:23.410
You have a poor poker face,
just like your master.

00:17:29.620 --> 00:17:32.540
I have many questions for you.

00:17:32.540 --> 00:17:35.500
Would you join us for a bit?

00:17:39.330 --> 00:17:41.200
Welcome to--

00:17:41.200 --> 00:17:43.660
Why, Lord Albert!

00:17:43.660 --> 00:17:45.200
Is Mr Eden in?

00:17:45.200 --> 00:17:47.410
He is inside...

00:17:48.750 --> 00:17:53.290
Well, Lord Albert.
What brings you here at this hour?

00:17:53.290 --> 00:17:57.410
I am asking a lady with whom I am becoming
closer to go to dinner with me,

00:17:57.410 --> 00:18:00.370
so I thought I would order
something a little fancy.

00:18:00.370 --> 00:18:03.950
It is likely to be a rather detailed order.

00:18:03.950 --> 00:18:07.910
Very well, then. Here, let us go inside.

00:18:07.910 --> 00:18:09.950
You can go home now.

00:18:09.950 --> 00:18:11.200
Yes, sir.

00:18:51.620 --> 00:18:59.250
Your lordship, please forgive the somewhat rough
methods I had to use to get you to come here.

00:18:59.250 --> 00:19:05.080
However, there is a gentleman here
who insists on seeing you alone.

00:19:08.000 --> 00:19:11.250
It has been too long, my lord.

00:19:16.870 --> 00:19:21.290
Are you certain you can grant my wish...

00:19:21.290 --> 00:19:23.160
...Sir William?

00:19:24.500 --> 00:19:28.370
Mr Eden, what you are proposing to do

00:19:28.370 --> 00:19:34.660
is unfortunately categorised
by this twisted world as a crime.

00:19:34.660 --> 00:19:37.870
Knowing this, does your
resolve remain unchanged?

00:19:57.370 --> 00:19:59.120
Very well.

00:20:00.790 --> 00:20:08.040
Then I, crime consultant William James
Moriarty, accept your request.

00:20:16.330 --> 00:20:20.370
Please be quick about it.
I only have one cigarette on me.

00:21:00.950 --> 00:21:02.500
Mr Eden?

00:21:03.750 --> 00:21:06.450
Come, let's be off.

00:21:23.040 --> 00:21:26.750
<i>An oath committed by souls assumed,</i>

00:21:26.750 --> 00:21:30.950
<i>with ideals that wallow in genetic karma</i>

00:21:44.950 --> 00:21:50.040
<i>Lie! Be resolute if you're going</i>
<i>to share your pain</i>

00:21:50.040 --> 00:21:52.290
<i>(Demonstrate your resolve)</i>

00:21:52.290 --> 00:21:55.790
<i>Like, dislike, you can't afford</i>
<i>to care either way</i>

00:21:55.790 --> 00:21:59.000
<i>It depends on the objective</i>
<i>(Making it happen is what's most important)</i>

00:21:59.000 --> 00:22:02.500
<i>The necessary evil of self-sacrifice</i>

00:22:02.500 --> 00:22:06.160
<i>is a righteous cause that no one can comprehend</i>

00:22:06.160 --> 00:22:09.910
<i>Take pride in the inviolable bonds shared</i>

00:22:09.910 --> 00:22:14.750
<i>among brothers who bear the same crime</i>

00:22:14.750 --> 00:22:18.410
<i>Make a chance trigger your inevitable stance</i>

00:22:18.410 --> 00:22:20.080
<i>and get drunk on your accomplishments</i>

00:22:20.080 --> 00:22:21.870
<i>at the end</i>

00:22:21.870 --> 00:22:25.040
<i>Don't believe in what you can see,</i>

00:22:25.040 --> 00:22:29.290
<i>in truths there's no point in knowing</i>
<i>(Whatever it takes)</i>

00:22:29.290 --> 00:22:35.870
<i>Defer to its own validity,</i>
<i>you only have one goal</i>

00:22:35.870 --> 00:22:37.370
<i>(Let me hear you say)</i>

00:22:39.750 --> 00:22:44.200
<i>You can't lie to yourself, come along with me</i>

00:22:47.160 --> 00:22:49.870
<i>It's all because there is no answer</i>

00:22:49.870 --> 00:22:52.250
<i>There is no turning back</i>

00:22:54.290 --> 00:22:57.040
Good morning, William.

00:22:59.950 --> 00:23:02.620
Have there been any interesting incidents?

00:23:02.620 --> 00:23:04.290
No.

00:23:04.290 --> 00:23:07.830
There's nothing in here about
an allegedly misbehaving earl,

00:23:07.830 --> 00:23:12.620
as well as his coachman,
being found brutally massacred,

00:23:12.620 --> 00:23:15.910
or anything like that, which would
set a Londoner hopping.

00:23:16.950 --> 00:23:18.700
I see.

00:23:20.910 --> 00:23:23.950
If one removes any trace
of an incident happening,

00:23:23.950 --> 00:23:28.660
then it isn't even recognised
as being an incident.

00:23:28.660 --> 00:23:30.290
In other words...

00:23:33.040 --> 00:23:35.250
...the perfect crime.

00:23:44.790 --> 00:23:51.000
Next time on <i>Moriarty the Patriot</i>:
"The Scarlet Eyes Act 1"
